description><link>https://daily.dev/posts/good-ol-times-rik9r6nec</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://api.daily.dev/r/riK9R6nec</guid><pubDate>Wed, 13 May 2026 06:15:00 GMT</pubDate><author>Denis Bolkovskis</author><category>ai</category><category>company-culture</category></item><item><title>Coding all the things manually, did it really happen?!</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--foaA6JGU--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2004&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description><link>https://daily.dev/posts/coding-all-the-things-manually-did-it-really-happen--zv0gdwu2b</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://api.daily.dev/r/ZV0GDWU2B</guid><pubDate>Mon, 11 May 2026 17:52:39 GMT</pubDate><author>Denis Bolkovskis</author><itunes:image href="https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--foaA6JGU--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2004"></itunes:image></item><item><title>Agents...</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--7l-7QfJN--/f_auto/v1777078566/posts/TTWMaAAoL?_a=BAMAMiWQ0&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description><link>https://daily.dev/posts/agents--gwbroggho</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://api.daily.dev/r/GWbroggho</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Apr 2026 01:01:31 GMT</pubDate><author>Michelle Galindo</author><itunes:image href="https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--7l-7QfJN--/f_auto/v1777078566/posts/TTWMaAAoL?_a=BAMAMiWQ0"></itunes:image></item><item><title>Linters are good</title><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--0PhhU9Ng--/f_auto/v1776356080/ugc/content_025ce7ed-b20d-4bb6-99d7-9f77bbdfa5cc?_a=BAMAMiWQ0&quot; alt=&quot;image.png&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://daily.dev/posts/linters-are-good-l32rmiea8</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://api.daily.dev/r/L32RmieA8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Apr 2026 17:01:13 GMT</pubDate><author>Özkan Pakdil</author><category>devops</category></item><item><title>New rules and guidelines</title><description>&lt;p&gt;Hi everyone! It’s been a while since we opened this squad and after &lt;strong&gt;6k members&lt;/strong&gt; and almost &lt;strong&gt;2k posts&lt;/strong&gt;, it’s time to update our rules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can see the new rules below, or just visit the &lt;a href=&quot;https://dly.to/GEIZObzVbLz&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener nofollow&quot;&gt;pinned post&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What We’re About&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Watercooler is all about:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Generating hilarity and nonsense&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Sharing delightful moments of distraction&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Casual off-topic discussions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Memes and dev humor&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Light-hearted debates (e.g., light mode vs. dark mode? 🌓)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Remember, as a public Squad, your posts might appear in the main daily.dev feed. Keep it fun, but keep it clean!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Rules (because even nonsense needs structure)&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be respectful and kind.&lt;/strong&gt; We don’t do hate here. 💜&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No self-promotion.&lt;/strong&gt; This isn’t the place to market yourself or your projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay on theme.&lt;/strong&gt; Keep it light, funny, and dev-culture related. Serious conversations belong elsewhere.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Don’t spam.&lt;/strong&gt; Quality over quantity, folks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No harmful content.&lt;/strong&gt; Viruses, IP grabbers, or any malicious content will get you permanently banned.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Watch your language.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Respect privacy.&lt;/strong&gt; Don’t post anyone’s personal information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Listen to the mods.&lt;/strong&gt; If a moderator asks you to stop something, please comply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep introductions to designated threads.&lt;/strong&gt; No standalone introduction posts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No product feedback or reading streak posts.&lt;/strong&gt; This isn’t the place for daily.dev feature discussions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No politics.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What We Want to See&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Your best (or worst) dev memes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Embarrassing dev stories&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Silly polls and light-hearted debates&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Casual chit-chat about dev life&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Remember, Watercooler is here for you to relax, laugh, and connect with fellow devs in a casual setting. Let’s keep it fun, friendly, and slightly ridiculous!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now, go forth and meme responsibly! 🎉&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description><link>https://daily.dev/posts/new-rules-and-guidelines-fnfb3ovyf</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://api.daily.dev/r/FNfb3OVYf</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Sep 2024 10:35:04 GMT</pubDate><author>Ido Shamun</author></item><item><title>Code of Conduct 🍄</title><description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/public/welcome_post&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hey there, fellow devs! Welcome to Watercooler, daily.dev’s first public Squad and your go-to spot for all things fun and non-professional in the dev world.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What We’re About&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Watercooler is all about:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Generating hilarity and nonsense&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Sharing delightful moments of distraction&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Casual off-topic discussions&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Memes and dev humor&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Light-hearted debates (e.g., light mode vs. dark mode? 🌓)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Remember, as a public Squad, your posts might appear in the main daily.dev feed. Keep it fun, but keep it clean!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;The Rules (because even nonsense needs structure)&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be respectful and kind.&lt;/strong&gt; We don’t do hate here. 💜&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No self-promotion.&lt;/strong&gt; This isn’t the place to market yourself or your projects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay on theme.&lt;/strong&gt; Keep it light, funny, and dev-culture related. Serious conversations belong elsewhere.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Don’t spam.&lt;/strong&gt; Quality over quantity, folks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No harmful content.&lt;/strong&gt; Viruses, IP grabbers, or any malicious content will get you permanently banned.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Watch your language.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Respect privacy.&lt;/strong&gt; Don’t post anyone’s personal information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Listen to the mods.&lt;/strong&gt; If a moderator asks you to stop something, please comply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep introductions to designated threads.&lt;/strong&gt; No standalone introduction posts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No product feedback or reading streak posts.&lt;/strong&gt; This isn’t the place for daily.dev feature discussions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No politics.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;What We Want to See&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Your best (or worst) dev memes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Embarrassing dev stories&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Silly polls and light-hearted debates&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li&gt;Casual chit-chat about dev life&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Remember, Watercooler is here for you to relax, laugh, and connect with fellow devs in a casual setting. Let’s keep it fun, friendly, and slightly ridiculous!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now, go forth and meme responsibly! 🎉&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description><link>https://daily.dev/posts/code-of-conduct--xxpptc1of</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://api.daily.dev/r/xxpPTc1Of</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Jun 2023 07:57:05 GMT</pubDate><author>Ido Shamun</author><itunes:image href="https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/public/welcome_post"></itunes:image></item></channel></rss>